<p>.08 <span class="emphasis"><em>Rehabilitation Expenditures Treated as Separate New Building</em></span>. For calendar year 2025, the per low-income unit qualified basis amount under § 42(e)(3)(A)(ii)(II) is $8,500.</p>

<p>.09 <span class="emphasis"><em>Low-Income Housing Credit</em></span>. For calendar year 2025, the amount used under § 42(h)(3)(C)(ii) to calculate the State housing credit ceiling for the low-income housing credit is the greater of (1) $3.00 multiplied by the State population, or (2) $3,455,000.</p>

<p>.10 <span class="emphasis"><em>Employee Health Insurance Expense of Small Employers</em></span>. For taxable years beginning in 2025, the dollar amount in effect under § 45R(d)(3)(B) is $33,300. This amount is used under § 45R(c) for limiting the small employer health insurance credit and under § 45R(d)(1)(B) for determining who is an eligible small employer for purposes of the credit.</p>

<p>.11 <span class="emphasis"><em>Exemption Amounts for Alternative Minimum Tax</em></span>. For taxable years beginning in 2025, the exemption amounts und/eable § 55(d)(1) are:</p>

